    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341-a1">

                <pb facs="0456" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg368"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vasquez to Mr.
                            Brown.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Honduras,<lb/>Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1904-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                                1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have had the honor to receive
                    the memorial and the documents related thereto of the claim of Mrs. Emma G.
                    Renton and Ella Miller Renton, presented to the Department at Washington, and
                    which originated in a crime which foreigners committed against Charles W. Renton
                    in Honduran territory.</p>
                <p>The claimants took steps in this direction in 1894, as you know, the year in
                    which the crime occurred.</p>
                <p>My Government is not only interested in arriving at a solution of this affair in
                    accordance with justice and right, but also in preserving the cordial relations
                    of friendship that bind it to the Government of the United States, and has given
                    me instructions to make known to your excellency that in due time there will be
                    forwarded the reply that the study of the documents and antecedents of the case
                    may bring forth.</p>
                <p>I cherish the hope that upon the return from the United States of His Excellency
                    Mr. Leslie Combs, he will come by way of this capital, when we can personally
                    take up this affair.</p>
                <p>With assurances, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mariano Vasques.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(<hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—The above-mentioned claims, and the
                        claim of the estate of Jacob Baiz, were settled on November 25, 1904, by the
                        subjoined agreement.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
